 ## Overview
-Procedural instancing for voxel blocks replaces baked mesh geometry with a compact instance record per voxel, resolving position, color, and occlusion in the vertex shader using a shared cube template [S1, S2, S3, S4, unofficial]. It differs from standard hardware instancing by computing visibility flags and clip distances procedurally in the vertex stage, allowing for custom setup logic such as face culling without CPU-side mesh generation [S1, S3, S4, unofficial].
+Procedural instancing for voxel blocks replaces baked mesh geometry with a compact instance record per voxel, resolving position, color, and occlusion in the vertex shader using a shared cube template [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, unofficial]. It differs from standard hardware instancing by computing per-instance transformations and visibility flags (such as face culling) dynamically within the vertex shader, allowing for custom setup logic without CPU-side mesh generation [S3, S4, unofficial]. This method significantly reduces memory usage compared to baked geometries but increases vertex workload for dense layouts because it submits whole cubes and discards hidden faces in the shader [S1, S5, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A structured buffer (SSBO/StructuredBuffer) containing per-voxel instance data (position, solidity/visibility, texture index, rotation). A shared vertex buffer containing a base geometry (typically a 24-vertex unit cube or a set of shape vertices).
-*   **Output:** Rasterized voxels. Non-solid voxels are clipped. Hidden faces of solid voxels are pushed outside the clip volume.
+*   **Input:** A structured buffer (SSBO/StructuredBuffer) containing per-voxel instance data (position, visibility, texture index, rotation) [S1, S3, S5, unofficial]. A shared vertex buffer containing a base geometry (typically a 24-vertex unit cube) [S1, S5, unofficial].
+*   **Output:** Rasterized voxels with correct position, orientation, texture, and occlusion culling [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, unofficial].
 
 **Data Structures:**
